<div class="wrap">
  <section id="start">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="mark">1</span>
      <h2>An agent is a loop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="two">
      <div>
        <p class="definition">
          <span class="def-label">Definition 1.1</span>
          A <em>coding agent</em> is a language model run in a loop, where each reply
          may ask for a tool &mdash; read a file, edit it, run a command &mdash; and
          each tool result is fed back as the next input. The loop stops when the
          model answers without asking for anything.
        </p>
        <p>
          That's the whole idea. Everything else in Tau &mdash; sessions,
          skills, the terminal UI &mdash; is built around this loop, not inside
          it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="ghost" href="/internals/agent-loop/"
            >Read the loop <span class="arr">&rarr;</span></a
          >
        </p>
      </div>
